  "narrative": "No assessments are due and no new independent validation requests remain. I therefore consolidated the final dataset-specific conclusions and reassessed several validation-exposed claims that had remained unresolved because their validation responses were near null or opposite sign: H7, H30, H34, H55, and H77 are changed to reject and closed because neither discovery nor validation gives robust evidence of a difference of at least 10 percent relative to the absolute outcome scale. The strongest supported finding in the supplied dataset is an association between feature_021=1 versus feature_021=0 and outcome_006. Because dependency scores are more negative for stronger dependency, positive signed mean-differences for direction +1 mean feature_021=1 cells have less negative outcome_006 scores, i.e. weaker dependency. The overall discovery estimate was +0.396 (95 percent interval +0.325 to +0.467), and independent validation was +0.435 (adjusted interval +0.334 to +0.536). The absolute mean outcome_006 scale is about 0.175, so the 10 percent operational benchmark is roughly 0.0175; both estimates are far above this benchmark and exclude the null. This is supported as an association in this dataset, not as causality or generalizable biology. The feature_021 outcome_006 association was also seen in many accepted subgroup contrasts, but the most informative internal localization involves feature_010. Accepted low-feature_010 simple contrasts are very large, including +0.810 (+0.781 to +0.839) at the feature_010 median split and +0.793 (+0.739 to +0.847) and +0.823 (+0.762 to +0.884) within feature_060=0 and feature_060=1 strata respectively. Corresponding accepted feature_010-high attenuation interactions are also large, including +0.789 (+0.674 to +0.904) overall and +0.399 (+0.148 to +0.650) and +0.513 (+0.274 to +0.751) within feature_060=0 and feature_060=1. These results support a dataset-specific effect-modification or localization pattern: the feature_021 outcome_006 association is extremely strong when feature_010 is low and strongly attenuated when feature_010 is high. They are not independent-validated, are post hoc in the feature_010 split, and do not establish that feature_010 causally modifies the association. The residual simple high-feature_010 contrasts remain uncertain and should not be promoted. The final negative picture is broad. Most simple predictor-outcome comparisons are null, too small, or imprecise. The feature_002 outcome_006 line is not supported after validation. Several discovery-only subgroup interactions failed validation, including the feature_043 median interaction for outcome_006 and the feature_057 interaction for outcome_006. The feature_008 outcome_008 association was only nominally discoverable and did not validate. Feature_048-level associations with outcome_009 in subgroups remain unsupported as clinically meaningful effects, and the H279 residual feature_065 outcome_015 association reversed in validation. I therefore treat smaller residual subgroup findings as noise unless they form a pre-specified, coherent, and externally replicated pattern. Unresolved uncertainty remains for small effects near the 10 percent threshold, especially the raw feature_021 contrast for outcome_005, some feature_065 residual associations with outcome_014 and outcome_015, and many deferred subgroup claims. These are either below the threshold, have intervals crossing null or the threshold, or lack validation. The main limitations are opaque predictor labels, correlated predictors, multiplicity, post hoc quantile splits, and the exhaustion of independent validation capacity. The next best analysis is not further broad subgroup mining but pre-specified model-based robustness and external replication of the feature_021 outcome_006 association and its feature_010 modification, including covariate adjustment, nonlinear modeling of feature_010, assay-level checks, causal-sensitivity diagnostics, and multiplicity-aware confirmation in independent data.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis iteration 23. No due validations; validation exhausted. Reassessed validated but unresolved claims H7, H30, H34, H55, H77 to reject and close. Main supported dataset-specific association: H146 feature_021=1 versus 0 associated with weaker outcome_006 dependency; validated effect +0.435, adjusted interval +0.334 to +0.536, far above the approximate 0.0175 10 percent absolute benchmark for outcome_006. Accepted localization: feature_010 low strata have very strong simple feature_021-outcome_006 contrasts, and feature_010 high strata show strong attenuation interactions; these are discovery-only and not causal. Main negative findings: feature_002 outcome_006 line unsupported; H272 and H261 interactions failed validation; H77, H240, and H279 not validated or reversed; most other predictors and outcomes show null, small, or imprecise effects. Next: model-based robustness, nonlinear feature_010 modification, covariate adjustment, causal-sensitivity checks, and external pre-specified replication rather than broad subgroup mining."
